 "statement": "Circular diagram: in the centre a four-legged hoofed animal with two backward-curving horns, ink only, facing left with its mouth at a green leafy sprig, standing on a green scalloped mound, with a short word in another script on its body (not read). Around it an inner ring of 5 and an outer ring of 10 women, each clothed (red, pink or green dresses, several with red or pale caps) and standing or set in a box-shaped tub (washed blue or green, hatched, striped or a dotted basket), each holding or tied to an eight-pointed star; figures in the lower half are upside down, feet toward the centre. Beside the striped tub at about 9 o'clock on the outer ring there are two small hatched rectangular blocks. The transcription's label lines between circular lines fall in blocks of 10 (f71r.2-11) and 5 (f71r.13-17), matching the 10 outer and 5 inner figures. Each figure carries its ring's block as label_group; which line goes with which figure cannot be fixed from line ids without reading the words, so labels are null. Clock positions are from the centre of the diagram, 12 = top of the scan. Filed under the M-L4 mandate because no PIC step was open for f71r; it is meant as the first of the folio's two independent annotations.",
